    <bpmn:process id="W_W3361" name="W3361. Industry Association Membership Strategy, Selection &amp; Dues Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual review; new association opportunity
Frequency: Annual + on opportunity
Volume: Portfolio of memberships (retail, chambers, supply-chain, sector)
Owner: Government Affairs Manager
Participants: Govt Affairs Mgr, VP Legal &amp; Compliance, affected business units, Procurement/Finance (links to VS-34/VS-17.1)
Source: workflow W3361 — Industry Association Membership Strategy, Selection &amp; Dues Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3361_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3361_Lane1" name="Govt Affairs Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3361_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3361_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3361_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3361_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3361_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3361_Start3" name="Annual review; new association opportunity">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3361_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3361_Task4" name="Govt Affairs Mgr maintain the membership strategy and portfolio: assess each…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Govt Affairs Mgr maintain the membership strategy and portfolio: assess each association&#x27;s value (advocacy access, benchmarking, standards, networking, brand) vs cost (dues, time); select/maintain/exit memberships
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3361_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3361_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3361_Task5" name="Govt Affairs Mgr/Procurement manage dues, contracts, and renewals (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Govt Affairs Mgr/Procurement manage dues, contracts, and renewals (links to VS-34.2); approve per authority matrix (links to VS-36); assign BuildRight representatives and engagement plan per association
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs Mgr / Procurement
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3361_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3361_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3361_Task6" name="Govt Affairs Mgr track membership utilization and ROI (W3367), and report the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Govt Affairs Mgr track membership utilization and ROI (W3367), and report the portfolio to leadership; coordinate labor-association engagement (ECOP/FWE) with labor relations (links to VS-84.3 W2893)
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3361_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3361_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3361_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3361_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-542 (ensure controlled execution — Industry &amp; Trade Association Relations (PA-104.2).) | - operational: ROI evaluation (W3367); operational: review
Owner: Government Affairs Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
